posixlib/clib: keep the link names of externs that libraries built with Scala Native 0.5.12 reference

Upstream (#5123, FreeBSD/OpenBSD/NetBSD support) added @name("scalanative_...") to externs that
already existed: socket, nanosleep, clock_gettime, sigaltstack and setlocale. The link name is part
of the extern's NIR global (Sig.Extern), so a library compiled against 0.5.12 that calls
socket.socket references Sig.Extern("socket"), which no longer exists:
"Unknown extern symbol scala.scalanative.posix.sys.socket$.socket". Keep the 0.5.12 names; the
scalanative_* C shims stay in the resources, unreferenced.

diff --git a/clib/src/main/scala/scala/scalanative/libc/locale.scala b/clib/src/main/scala/scala/scalanative/libc/locale.scala
index 4630d36..47ee022 100644
--- a/clib/src/main/scala/scala/scalanative/libc/locale.scala
+++ b/clib/src/main/scala/scala/scalanative/libc/locale.scala
@@ -79,7 +79,6 @@ private[scalanative] trait locale {
 
   def localeconv(): Ptr[lconv] = extern
 
-  @name("scalanative_setlocale")
   def setlocale(category: CInt, locale: CString): CString = extern
 }
 
